Build-time fixes adapting the fork to 1.96.0 internals (the fork was
authored against 1.97-dev master). Conflict resolutions for the
attribute table (2-arg rustc_attr! shim), ty_utils/abi.rs (FnSig fields)
and check_attr.rs are folded into their originating patches; this commit
carries the remaining drift fixes:

- rustc_attr_parsing codegen_attrs.rs: `rustcc_noargs_attr!` adds
  `ON_DUPLICATE = OnDuplicate::Error` (1.96.0's NoArgsAttributeParser
  requires it; defaulted away after 1.96).
- rustc_symbol_mangling itanium.rs/swift.rs: `FnSig::abi`/`c_variadic`
  are fields in 1.96.0 (method-call forms are 1.97-isms).
- rustc_codegen_ssa mir/block.rs: `mk_fn_sig` is 5-arg and `FnSig`
  exposes c_variadic/safety/abi fields (1.97 bundled them into
  `fn_sig_kind` + a 3-arg ctor).
- rustc_mir_transform cxx_throws_wrap.rs: resolve the `From` trait via
  `get_diagnostic_item(sym::From)` (it's a diagnostic item in 1.96.0;
  became `LangItem::From` later); drop the now-unused LangItem import.

Validated: stage1 builds, all 9 fork probes pass, and
examples/subclass_cpp_base (subclass + virtual destructor) runs green
on the 1.96.0 toolchain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
